From 619a1dab1bdd04592e759be527cf25eb691ad0aa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John R Reeves III <johnreevesiii@outlook.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 06:14:19 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 03/22] wasm: drop code compiled only without JIT_PROD_BUILD

The production build (build-prod.sh) always defines JIT_PROD_BUILD.
Every guard naming it is '#ifndef JIT_PROD_BUILD' or an '&&'
conjunction containing '!defined(JIT_PROD_BUILD)', so each guarded
branch is dead in production. This commit removes those branches and
keeps any '#else' branch unguarded; one '#elif FLY_REGIONS_LIVE'
becomes '#if FLY_REGIONS_LIVE'. The result is what the preprocessor
already saw in a production build, so prod behaviour is unchanged.

Removed: the dev test harness entry points, console diagnostics,
counters, PC traces and probes in 16 files (2786 lines). The
FLY_PVR_DIAG, FLY_RETRO_DIAG and FLY_RELEASE_BUILD switches stay.

Done mechanically by a conditional-stripping script that refuses any
JIT_PROD_BUILD guard it cannot decide (no '||' at the top level, no
'#ifdef JIT_PROD_BUILD'). Not compiled: the build is pending approval.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MGX7KQ5gfrWApgW64pZbQ5
